# gscrm

Read and write the LBV Google Sheets CRM via the service account.

Sheet name is controlled by `GSCRM_SHEET_NAME` env var (default: `Sheet1`). Never hard-code the sheet name.

## Usage

```bash
node ~/.openclaw/tools/gscrm.js '<json>'
```

## Operations

### Read rows

```bash
# Most recent 5 rows
node ~/.openclaw/tools/gscrm.js '{"op":"read","limit":5}'

# Find by Stripe session ID
node ~/.openclaw/tools/gscrm.js '{"op":"read","session_id":"cs_live_xxx"}'

# Find by email
node ~/.openclaw/tools/gscrm.js '{"op":"read","email":"customer@example.com"}'
```

### Append a new row

```bash
node ~/.openclaw/tools/gscrm.js '{"op":"append","row":{"Timestamp":"2026-05-08T10:00:00Z","Email":"customer@example.com","Full Name":"Jane Smith","Tier":"T3","Payment Status":"Paid","Fulfillment Status":"Awaiting Info"}}'
```

### Update fields on an existing row

```bash
# Update by session ID
node ~/.openclaw/tools/gscrm.js '{"op":"update","session_id":"cs_live_xxx","fields":{"Fulfillment Status":"Complete","Notes / Next Action":"USB shipped 2026-05-08"}}'

# Update by row number
node ~/.openclaw/tools/gscrm.js '{"op":"update","row_number":15,"fields":{"Payment Status":"Paid"}}'
```

### Delete a row (use sparingly — only for cleanup/test rows)

```bash
node ~/.openclaw/tools/gscrm.js '{"op":"delete","row_number":42}'
```

## Column reference (34 columns)

```
Timestamp | Email | Full Name | Phone | Tier | Lead Source | Discount Code | Discount %
Amount Paid | Stripe Session ID | Payment Method | Street Address | City | State / Province
Postal Code | Country | Jarvis Name | Jarvis Personality | Personality Notes | Preferred Platform
Niche / Industry | Workflows | Current Tools | Revenue Goal | Hardware Config | Additional Notes
PayPal Return Tier | Payment Status | Fulfillment Status | Questionnaire Complete
USB Built | Hardware Ordered / Tracking # | Setup Session Scheduled | Notes / Next Action
```

## Output

Success: `{"ok":true,...}` with operation-specific data
Failure: `{"ok":false,"error":"..."}`

## Rules

- Always use column names exactly as listed above — case-sensitive
- Never hard-code the sheet name; always rely on GSCRM_SHEET_NAME env var
- For `append`, include at minimum: Timestamp, Email, Tier, Payment Status
- For `delete`, only use on `[TEST]` rows or after explicit Andrey approval
- If `ok` is false, report the full error to Apex before retrying
- Read before update if you're unsure of the current state
